      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-306041",
      ":question/problem": "The ages, in years, of $20$ trees in a park were recorded, and the mean, median, range, and standard deviation were calculated. Later, it was discovered that the youngest tree\u2019s age had been reported as $5$ years too high.\nWhich of the following statistics remains unchanged when recalculated using the corrected age?\n\n1. Mean\n2. Median\n3. Range\n4. Standard deviation"
